Based on the search results, here's a comprehensive overview of setting up **next-intl** with layout, metadata, and `generateStaticParams`:

## Complete next-intl Setup

### 1. Routing Configuration

Create a `routing.ts` file as a central place to define your routing configuration using `defineRouting` from 'next-intl/routing' with a list of supported locales and a default locale.

### 2. Middleware Setup

Once you have your routing configuration in place, you can use it to set up a proxy using `createMiddleware` from 'next-intl/middleware'.

### 3. Layout with generateStaticParams

Since we are using a dynamic route segment for the `[locale]` param, we need to use `generateStaticParams` so that the routes can be rendered at build time.(no content)The layout validates that the incoming locale parameter is valid and sets up static generation for all defined locales using `setRequestLocale`.

Example layout structure:
```typescript
// app/[locale]/layout.tsx
import { setRequestLocale } from 'next-intl/server';
import { routing } from '@/i18n/routing';
import { notFound } from 'next/navigation';

export function generateStaticParams() {
  return routing.locales.map((locale) => ({locale}));
}

export default async function LocaleLayout({
  children,
  params,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  params: Promise<{locale: string}>;
}) {
  const {locale} = await params;

  if (!routing.locales.includes(locale as any)) {
    notFound();
  }

  setRequestLocale(locale);
  return children;
}
```

### 4. Internationalized Metadata with generateMetadata

To internationalize metadata like the page title, you can use functionality from next-intl in the `generateMetadata` function that can be exported from pages and layouts, using `getTranslations` from 'next-intl/server'.(no content)By passing an explicit locale to the awaitable functions from next-intl, you can make the metadata handler eligible for static rendering if you're using locale-based routing.

Example:
```typescript
export async function generateMetadata({params}) {
  const {locale} = await params;
  const t = await getTranslations({locale, namespace: 'Metadata'});

  return {
    title: t('title'),
    description: t('description')
  };
}
```

### 5. Important Notes

You need to call `setRequestLocale` in every page and every layout that you intend to enable static rendering for since Next.js can render layouts and pages independently.(no content)`setRequestLocale` needs to be called before you invoke any functions from next-intl like `useTranslations` or `getMessages`.(no content)The `generateStaticParams` function can be used in combination with dynamic route segments to statically generate routes at build time instead of on-demand at request time.


